Change Values by Assigning a Value in SimTalk
You can change the settings, which you can select in or type into the dialogs of the objects, by assigning a
value to an object attribute in SimTalk.
To set a constant Processing Time of three minutes, you can type the setting below into the dialog.
Or you can type this instruction into a Method:
Paths in SimTalk Instructions
In the example we inserted the material flow object MyStation into the Frame called Models. This is why
the title bar of the station MyStation shows the absolute path .Models.MyPlantAnytown.MyStation.
As we inserted the Method named MyMethodMyStation into the same Frame as the station
MyStation, which the title bar of the Method also shows, we can type in the instruction
MyStation.ProcTime := 180 or MyStation.ProcTime := 3:00 and do not have to type the
entire path, i.e., .Models.MyPlantAnytown.MyStation.ProcTime := 180.
Within the instruction MyStation.ProcTime := 180 the term MyStation designates the object for
which the instruction applies. This is followed by a separator, namely a period ., followed by the name
of the attribute which we want to change, ProcTime in our case. The value after the assignment
operator :=, without a blank space between the colon and the equal sign, is assigned to the value of the
attribute while the is being executed, 180, i.e., three minutes in our case.
To set the Exit Strategy > Linear sequence, you can select it in the drop-down list and then type the
numbers of the successors of the Station into the List that clicking the button Open List opens.
Change Values by Assigning a Value in SimTalk
