Change Values with the AttributeExplorer
Instead of opening the dialog of each and every material flow object in your model and entering values
for a single attribute or for a number of attributes into the text boxes, you can define which attributes of
which objects the AttributeExplorer gets.
Using the AttributeExplorer 
  you can manage the attributes defining the settings of the individual
stations in your simulation model at a single location. You can then enter different values for the
capacities, the times, etc. Plant Simulation writes these values back to the dialogs of the objects and
uses them in your simulation model. You can also export this settings table as a tab-delimited text file
and import this file into the AttributeExplorer of another simulation model, thus using identical settings in
several of your simulation models.
You can also use the AttributeExplorer to find objects of the type you define, to find attributes, for example
the position of a number of objects. You can then align them in the Frame, etc.
Compare Set Parameters with the AttributeExplorer
Compare Specify the Attributes You Want to View or Change
