Find Any Source Code in a Method
You can find any text, which you entered as source code into any Method object which you inserted into
your simulation model or in any user-defined attribute of data type method.
Proceed as follows:
1. Select Source Code from the left drop-down list.
2. Enter any text or value contained within the source code of a Method in the search scope.
3. Repeat steps 4 to 10 described under Find the Name of an Object.
4. When you select Ignore Inherited Name or Text Plant Simulation then only finds the original source
code you entered into a Method object, and not the source code in derived or duplicated objects.
5. Click Find.
6. To open the Method that Plant Simulation found and to jump to the first occurrence of the item,
double-click it in the results pane. Double-clicking or selecting Open again jumps to the next
occurrence of the found item.
To jump to the previous occurrence in the source code, hold down Shift and double-click.
Find Any Source Code in a Method
